    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-212114",
      "sequence_position": 9,
      "problem": "Which of the following is the graph representing the relation $R=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<81\\}?$",
      "worked_solution": "A binary relation can be visualized using a plot (or graph), where \n\n- the first set goes along the horizontal line,\n\n- the second set goes along the vertical line,\n\n- each pair $(x,y)$ from the relation defines a point with coordinates $(x,y)$ on the plot.\n\nIn our case, the plot contains all the points in ${R}^{2}$ for which \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<81.\n$$\n\nThese are the points that lie *inside* the circle of radius $9$ centered at the origin.\n\nFinally, since we have a strict inequality, the points on the circle must be excluded from the plot, which we depict by using a *dashed* curve:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14120255/assets/4e08efd6af5e38ed82c0c1659088620b673afbfad5a751c07a492dd0fc4c497c.png)",
